WEBVTT

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.250
If you have something to say,
why don't you come out and say it?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.620
No, I don't.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.210
I was just wondering
if you could actually go through with it.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.390
Would you care to find out right now?

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.970
Scary!

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:19.300
Where are your wings?
Are they tucked away inside your body?

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.800
I was told to touch Canopus.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.520
So, I made contact with you.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.270
Touch what? Told by who?

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.240
Canopus. That's what we call old people
who show us the way.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.370
What a coincidence. I've been looking
for a murderous little punk myself.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.750
Where is Yuna?

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.620
Yuna?

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:01.550
Is Yuna the "IIII" you've spent your life
apart from...

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.560
my good number 13?

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.730
So, has she noticed the marks
you've been leaving for her?

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:18.740
From the looks of it,
it seems like she hasn't answered yet.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.740
And after all your effort
with those murders...

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:25.320
Your girlfriend is pretty cold.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:31.170
The only people I kill
are those who deserve to die.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.460
How upstanding of you.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.130
Here. Want one?

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.640
I guess you never had any grownups around

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.600
to tell you not to be so full of yourself.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.930
What do you know?

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.440
Nothing, I guess.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.570
But I do know
what that mark of yours means.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.200
That's not a "B,"

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:08.070
that's a 13 in Arabic numerals

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:11.160
and the Roman numeral four
only used on clocks, right?

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.790
Two numbers overlapping.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:19.340
The 13 is you, and she is the IIII, right?

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:25.340
It's probably a code
only the two of you would recognize,

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.800
and Killer B has kept killing murderers
as a way to spread it.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:37.100
It was all to let this girl you can't find
know that you're alive.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:42.730
Every time you killed someone,
it was like you were shouting.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.570
"I'm right here!"

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.780
Where is Yuna?

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:56.960
Goodness, kids these days are so greedy,
with no concept of give and take.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.130
Anyway, you must've brought me here
because you had something to ask.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.090
Well, I have questions for you, too.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.850
I'm not interested in playing word games
with you.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.810
If you know, tell me where Yuna--

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.940
Tomorrow at 10:00.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.650
You know where Heian-ji is?

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.610
It's an Oriental-style Buddhist temple.
In Ward Eight.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.570
I'll tell you everything then.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.450
Hey! Tell me here!

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.410
There's something I need to show you.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.080
I'll bring it tomorrow. Don't be late.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:44.010
ROYAL POLICE, STORAGE WAREHOUSE

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.930
What is this place?

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.640
Archives Division.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.310
Oops.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.820
Where is it, where is it?

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.490
Keith worked here?

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.500
Yeah. For eight years.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.500
All by himself.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.050
What was the reason?

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.550
Why was he sent here?

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:34.390
During the trial, he abducted the murderer
Dead Kyle from the hospital he was in

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.560
and tortured him without authorization.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.270
He did what?

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:52.990
How did it go?

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.700
They've begun the paperwork
for an arrest warrant.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:59.120
We'll be sent out after Keith, too.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:03.960
Your nail.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.210
Where is Lily?

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.340
In the building.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.770
It's a shame about Jean.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.440
Yes.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.150
You're here about Keith Flick, right?

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:29.690
Is he a suspect?

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.480
For the time being.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.120
Then, you're here for me?

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.580
Yes. I heard from Boris
about how you and Keith are old friends.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.540
I've known him since boarding school.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.010
We can't shake each other.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:50.710
Doctor, do you also think Keith did this?

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.380
Do you?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:54.670
I don't think he did it.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:55.760
I see.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:59.810
Um, please tell me everything
you can about--

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:05.150
The Keith Flick I know
is an exceedingly dull man.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:11.230
Since he can predict what lies ahead,
he can't really act in the moment.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:16.370
Um, so what you're saying is,
this incident doesn't seem premeditated.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.120
Therefore, Keith couldn't have done it.
Is that what you meant?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.280
I don't know the particulars,

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:27.710
but if he's under suspicion,
he probably didn't do it.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.840
He couldn't do anything so careless.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:34.050
You don't mean "wouldn't"?

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.760
No, I mean couldn't.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:39.930
Interesting.

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:44.150
Just like always.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:45.610
Yes?

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:50.480
For as long as I've known him,
good hearts have always been drawn to him.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:54.570
In spite of his being so unpleasant.
It's the strangest thing.

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:57.530
You're one such person, I see.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:00.700
U-Um...

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.200
That will do for now.
Thank you for your time!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.540
You know...

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:10.000
maybe you really do resemble her.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.380
Excuse me?

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.480
Hey!

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:37.740
So carefree,
even though you're a wanted criminal.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:41.040
Being on the run leaves you
with a lot of down time.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.790
Did you bring it?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.830
Can't you see? It's on my back.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.330
Sorry. Thanks as always.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.590
Did Jean really kill himself?

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.340
-His memories?
-They'd been altered.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.060
Boy, this runs deep.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.800
Don't do anything crazy.
I won't be able to help you out forever.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:07.060
Eric already suspects
that I'm up to something.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:10.810
Don't worry about it. It'll probably end.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.310
And soon.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.400
I'm being forced to play along with It

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.450
Probably, anyway.
I'm being forced to play along with It

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.360
I'm being forced to play along with It

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.240
I'm being forced to play along with It

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:27.160
But what happens afterwards?

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:44.220
I'll capture Lohengrin, trust me.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.860
Is there a problem?

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:06.120
You know there is.
We didn't anticipate any of this.

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:11.460
That's precisely why.
We didn't expect Lohengrin's abilities.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:15.630
So, we'll counter the unexpected
with the unexpected.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.420
What if someone dies?

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.630
Just sit back and watch.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:38.740
WARD EIGHT, HEIAN-JI

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:08.050
You came.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:10.350
Your name.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.060
You have a name, don't you?

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.400
Tell me what it is.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.490
Koku.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.040
I'm Keith.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:27.110
I know.

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:28.700
Of course you do.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.950
Where do I start?

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:34.880
Relax.
Yuna's-

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:35.880
Relax.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.290
If you're alive, so is she.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.260
You better not be guessing.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:49.930
If I said "Jaula Blanca Institute,"
would you be more likely to believe me?

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.390
It all began at the Jetblack.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:00.850
At the end of the 16th Century,

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:05.690
13 fossilized skeletons were discovered
in the ruins at the top of the mountain.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:11.160
The scientists of the day classified
the bizarre winged skeletons

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.960
as the progenitors of humanity

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.660
and were fossils of gods
that flourished in the ancient past.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.800
So began the project
to restore these gods.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:26.800
The king and government realized they
could exploit the project politically.

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:31.220
So,
to refill the country's depleted coffers,

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:34.940
they solicited donations under the pretext
of resurrecting these gods

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:37.980
and built a huge research facility.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:43.950
Its name was the Jaula Blanca
Royal Scientific Institute.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:49.280
Top scientists
and the cutting-edge technology of the day

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:53.160
were brought there
in the name of resurrecting the gods.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:56.870
However...

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:01.380
there were only corrupted researchers
who had grown drunk on the huge donations

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.250
and days spent on trivialities.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:07.960
Without a particular plan,
they began an inbreeding program

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.220
which produced malformed, insane offspring
they called the Promising Ones,

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.680
which they disposed of.

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:18.020
That so-called research was repeated
again and again for several centuries.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:24.400
When rumors began circulating that this
unsuccessful research would be terminated,

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:29.400
one of the researchers went
before the king and made a proposal.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:33.870
"I will create an organization that
will intentionally manipulate the balance

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.990
of fear and tranquility
inside and outside the kingdom.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:43.080
I will develop the human assets required
to carry out the project at Jaula Blanca."

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:49.130
And so, the Promising Ones,
who had been derided as failures,

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:53.680
were sent to the royal government
to be special intelligence agents

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.260
that would create chaos and order.

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:00.020
Their work would go on
to have a profound effect.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:04.070
They're now known... as Market Maker.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.650
Because of this, the institute survives

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:13.070
as a facility that develops weapons
of carnage for their government patrons.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.700
Ironically, though,

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:20.670
it was at this point that their research
into the gods leapt forward.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:25.380
Two lives were born
that showed them the way to success.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.840
But at that point, something happened.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.060
Yuna?

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:41.560
Yuna?

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.060
Yuna! Yuna!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.530
Yuna!

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:48.270
Yuna!

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.900
Yuna! Yuna!

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.950
Yuna!

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:04.370
All I remember is gunfire
and a burnt smell.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.840
How do you know about me?

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:15.720
It's written "Kurohane" (Black Wings),
but it's read "Koku," huh?

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:18.720
That's just like him.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:23.060
Have you heard of the Jetblack Epitaph?

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:25.440
It's at the top of Mt. Cremona.

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:31.820
With advances in genetic research
and the deciphering of that inscription,

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.700
their research made
a quantum leap forward.

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:40.240
It contained a record of the abilities
and form of the gods' bones.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:46.040
It was the arrival from Japan
of three cellular biologists

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:49.750
that brought about the birth of you
and your guardians.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.050
One of those three...

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:53.970
was Dr. Kazama.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:59.140
Full name, Heath Kazama Flick.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:03.560
My father.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:08.650
And...

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:13.980
the one who first managed to decode
that inscription, at the age of 12,

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.120
was me.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:27.020
How many have you killed
with that hand you stole?

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:41.700
How much blood have you seen
with that eye you stole?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:54.840
How many crimes have you fled from
on that leg you stole?

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.840
They're pretty amazing, all right.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:32.000
Don't. Don't!

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:34.290
Don't kill her, Koku!

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:36.710
Stop it!

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:47.850
It can't be.

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:52.400
Yuna!

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:54.110
How dare you!

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.990
Your time of atonement is at hand.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:16.370
It's me, Yuna.

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:21.510
You killed them!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.340
Decide it together.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:31.190
You killed all my classmates
at Jaula Blanca! All of my friends!

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:35.190
Will you be killed by your most beloved?

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.640
I'll never forgive you!

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.190
Or will you kill your most beloved?

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:42.520
You're wrong, Yuna.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:43.070
Shut up!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:44.530
Yuna!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.410
It's time.

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:11.890
This ends it.

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:18.190
Yuna.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:26.110
I found you.

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:35.790
When Canopus shines bright,
to the right is a new First,

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:38.620
illegitimate spawn of the gods.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:43.420
Wings of pure madness
will bring low the ephemeral people,

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:47.800
and the howls of the dead
will bring order to their brethren.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:02.810
To the left, another Fourth.

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.690
A cycle of evil slaughter.

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:09.900
The moon of carnage traces out
its eternal ellipse,

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:13.990
and the hour the ash-colored dragon
beats its wings will come at last.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:17.920
People of the black bones,
gather ye together.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.420
Koku?

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:43.770
Koku!

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:50.740
Where have you been?
I've been waiting so long.

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:25.530
Someday I’ll be gone

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:34.120
To somewhere that we belong

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:39.500
And god has never played his role

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:43.790
Because I’m the one who saves my soul

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:48.920
It is a perfect world we’re longing for

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:52.050
So long...

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:22.710
Cursed shadows haunt and gather

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:26.340
In the city of no answer

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:30.630
as we follow endless questions

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:34.550
hands up in the same reflection

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:38.470
just used to be
Sometimes we try to feel how things

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:42.600
in yesterdays

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:46.690
No one ever make it better, no one ever lives forever

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:50.070
Wake me up and let me go

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:58.280
Someday I’ll be gone

00:23:58.280 --> 00:24:04.370
To somewhere we all belong

00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:07.130
For so long
